 # Customer Manager

 A small Spring Boot + Vaadin Flow application listing customers in a lazily
-loaded `Grid`.
+loaded `Grid`, with a name and status filter that lives in the URL.

 ```text
 src/main/java/com/example/
   Application.java                    Spring Boot entry point
   customers/
     domain/Customer.java              the record shown in the grid
+    domain/CustomerFilter.java        what the list is narrowed down to
     domain/CustomerRepository.java    paged, read-only access to customers.csv
     domain/CustomerSort.java          a sort instruction the repository understands
+    domain/NameSearch.java            how typed text is compared with a name
     service/CustomerService.java      what the UI talks to
     ui/CustomerListView.java          the view at /
 ```

+Both filters are part of the backend query, so the grid still holds one page of
+rows at a time and the matching count still comes from a count query. The filter
+is mirrored into the address bar as `?name=…&status=…` with `replaceState`, so a
+narrowed list can be bookmarked or shared without filling up the browser
+history.
+
 The 500 customers live in `src/main/resources/customers.csv` and are loaded once
 at startup.

